# Per-project CLAUDE.md TEMPLATE
# Copy this into a repo as `<repo>/CLAUDE.md`, fill the <...> placeholders, delete these two comment lines.
# It loads automatically in every session of THAT repo — for opus AND claude-glm.
# Keep it lean (<~40 lines); it rides in the cached prefix every turn.

# CLAUDE.md — <project name>

<one-line purpose, e.g. "Intraday options backtester + live trader.">

## Structure (where things live)
- <src/...>        — <what>
- <src/...>        — <what>
- <tests/>         — <test suite>
- <config/ or .env>— <config; do not read secrets>

## Navigation rules (apply always — token discipline)
- Use **serena** `find_symbol` / `get_symbols_overview` / go-to-def to locate code.
  Do NOT read whole files, and never read node_modules / dist / build / lockfiles / .env.
- Read only with `offset`/`limit` when you must; never re-read a file already in context.
- **Edit only the files named in the task.** Don't explore beyond the scope you were given.
- Prefer a scoped grep/symbol lookup over opening many files.

## Build / test
- Install: <cmd>
- Test:   <exact cmd, e.g. `pytest tests/ -q`>   ← run this to verify changes
- Lint/format: <cmd>

## Risk-critical (Opus review mandatory)
- <order routing / position sizing / money-moving logic / auth-secrets>: even if GLM wrote it,
  it MUST be reviewed by Opus before it lands. Never skip this gate.

## Notes
- Secrets live in env vars / git-ignored files — never read or print them.
- One-time per repo: run **serena onboarding** so it caches a project overview (persists across sessions).
